# Local dev needs none of this - `./mvnw quarkus:dev` works out of the box
# against DynamoDB Local (see ../docker-compose.yml) using the checked-in
# throwaway dev JWT keypair. These are the overrides that matter in
# staging/production, sourced from AWS Secrets Manager at container start
# (see infra/modules/backend-service and docs/runbooks/secrets-rotation.md).
# Copy to .env and export before running outside a container if you need to
# reproduce a production-like configuration locally.

# In ECS, the *_PEM variables below are injected as `secrets` (Secrets
# Manager-backed) and docker-entrypoint.sh writes them to these paths before
# the JVM starts, since Fargate has no native secret-to-file mount. Set the
# PEM variables to reproduce that locally instead of the path variables.
OFC_JWT_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=/app/secrets/privateKey.pem
OFC_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY_PATH=/app/secrets/publicKey.pem
# OFC_JWT_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----..."
# OFC_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY_PEM="-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----..."

# Standard Quarkus/MicroProfile env var overrides (mapped from
# quarkus.*/ofc.* properties in application.properties), useful when running
# the container image directly instead of via Terraform-managed ECS task
# definitions:
# QUARKUS_HTTP_PORT=8080
# OFC_DYNAMODB_REGION=us-east-1
# OFC_DYNAMODB_TABLE_PREFIX=ofc-prod-
# QUARKUS_HTTP_CORS_ORIGINS=https://play.ofc-poker.example.com
